This is a modifed calculator.py with some comments, that works both
with pre 1.4 JDK AWT and JDK 1.4 AWT, addressing the intervened mechanics
change. It is surely not the be-all about key event capturing and focus issues,
but it makes the example work as it worked with JDK 1.3.

With JDK 1.4 Sun has changed the way key event dispatching and focus are managed.
http://java.sun.com/j2se/1.4/docs/api/java/awt/doc-files/FocusSpec.html
Succintly, prior to JDK 1.4  top level windows received "always" key event, now
key events go to a KeyboardFocusManager that dispatches only to the focus owner
(which is not in general/always the top frame) or to explicitly set chained
dispatchers. This makes no difference for textfields etc which receive focus
upon editing, but it does in our case.
